@startuml
title Post-trade review — versioned Zone-aligned state machine

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

state "Pending" as Pending {
  state "risk_evidence: over_policy | unavailable" as PendingUrgent
  state "risk_evidence: within_policy" as PendingRoutine
}

state "Reviewed" as Reviewed {
  state "method: auto\n(one-click, evidence-driven)" as Auto
  state "method: manual\n(current 12-criterion assessment)" as Manual
}

state "Reclassified" as Reclassified <<choice>>

[*] --> PendingUrgent : import position\nrisk evidence over_policy / unavailable
[*] --> PendingRoutine : import position\nrisk evidence within_policy

PendingUrgent --> Auto : Approve (one click)
PendingRoutine --> Auto : Approve (one click)
PendingUrgent --> Manual : Full assessment
PendingRoutine --> Manual : Full assessment
Auto --> Manual : Full assessment\n(upgrades / replaces the auto review)

Auto --> PendingUrgent : Retract**\n(back to evidence-driven pending)
Auto --> PendingRoutine : Retract**

Manual --> Manual : Correct\n(new revision, prior superseded,\nhard-rule re-snapshotted)

Pending --> Reclassified : membership change
Reviewed --> Reclassified : membership change\n(review superseded)
Reclassified --> [*] : new logical_trade_id,\nre-enters at [*] fresh

note bottom of Reviewed
  Both Auto and Manual count toward
  current pillar scores / readiness roadmap
  when rubric_version = zone_v2.
  Earlier rubric assessments are converted once
  to zone_v2 with neutral new Psychology grades.
  Only Manual can record violation tags
  or hard-rule events.
end note

note right of PendingUrgent
  "Requires review" tab
end note
note right of PendingRoutine
  "Auto-reviewed" (pending) tab
end note
note left of Auto
  Tagged "Auto" under the "Reviewed" tab
end note
note left of Manual
  Tagged "Manual" under the "Reviewed" tab
end note

legend right
  ** Retract is a NEW capability proposed by
  this redesign — not present in the current
  implementation. Confirm before implementing.
endlegend

@enduml
